  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Patchoulane may be associated with ME-180 through a series of target relationships involving CD276 antigen. CD276 antigen is a target of multiple compounds, including Tumidulin and Prudomestin, as well as Patchoulane itself. These compounds are all linked to ME-180, indicating a potential pathway where Patchoulane could exert its effects through CD276 antigen, which in turn interacts with ME-180. The scores for all three paths are consistent, suggesting a strong and reliable relationship across different molecular targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Patchoulane and ME-180 through the CD276 antigen, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The consistency in scores across different paths strengthens the conclusion, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance of this relationship.",
